# Pig Animations (single GLB)

All pig clips live in **`public/models/pig/pig.glb`**. Registry: `PIG_MODEL` + `PIG_CLIPS` in `src/constants/models.ts`.

The GLB Armature is **cm-scaled (0.01)**. `fitSkinnedToHeight` must call `updateMatrixWorld(true)` and use `PIG_TARGET_HEIGHT` (~1.65m).

## Clip names (inside pig.glb)

| Key | Clip name | Loop |
|-----|-----------|------|
| walk / walkGun | Walking | yes |
| run | Running | yes |
| aim / shoot | Walk_Backward_While_Shooting | yes |
| catch | Leap_Right_and_Catch | no |
| deathAbdominal / deathShot | Dead | no |

## In-place clips + world locomotion

Walk / run / shoot clips do **not** travel. `update-soldiers.ts` writes `soldier.position`.

- Patrol (`biped`): `PIG_WALK_SPEED`, face velocity.
- Flee (`cowardly`): `Running`, `PIG_RUN_SPEED`, drop weapon.
- Catch (`catcher`): `Leap_Right_and_Catch` when the drone is close and low (`CATCH_RANGE` / `CATCH_ALTITUDE`).
- Shoot: `Walk_Backward_While_Shooting`, back away from the drone, **AK parented to `RightHand`**.
- Dead: `Dead`.

## Component pattern

- `PigAnimatedModel` — `SkeletonUtils.clone`, `useAnimations` on the cloned mesh ref, crossfade clips.
- AK is a `WeaponAk` that follows the `RightHand` bone (world → pig-local). Visible only while aiming/shooting.

## FPV ram

Contact is a **body capsule**, not distance-to-feet:

- Horizontal: `RAM_HORIZ` (~1.7)
- Vertical: drone Y between ground and `PIG_TARGET_HEIGHT + RAM_ALT_MARGIN`

Ram kills **every** pig-mesh soldier (including red-tinted ones). Level 1 spawns reds that use the same GLB — do not require `s.pig === true`. Then `checkExplosion` at the impact.

## AI roles (`setup-level.ts`)

- ~40% `cowardly` — run away when the drone is within flee range.
- ~half of the rest `catcher` — leap/catch when the drone flies near and low.
- Remaining — shoot with AK.
